1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,953
Get ready for one of the most jaw-dropping drives in America!

2
00:00:06,953 --> 00:00:09,972
A highway that crosses right over a waterfall.

3
00:00:09,972 --> 00:00:14,172
A mountain pass at eleven thousand feet with barely a guardrail.

4
00:00:14,172 --> 00:00:17,650
And a whole town that's a National Historic Landmark!

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:24,483
This is the Million Dollar Highway: just 24 miles, but every single one is a showstopper.

6
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:29,110
And stick around, because the full trip planner is waiting at the end!

7
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:31,561
Here's the game plan!

8
00:00:31,561 --> 00:00:38,637
We start in Ouray, stop at Bear Creek Falls, climb over Red Mountain Pass, and roll into Silverton.

9
00:00:38,637 --> 00:00:39,280
Let's go!

10
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:47,093
Welcome to Ouray, tucked into a box canyon with thirteen-thousand-foot peaks on every side!

11
00:00:47,093 --> 00:00:53,580
Before you hit the road, soak in the hot springs pool and walk out to Box Cañon Falls.

12
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,390
Trust me, it's worth it!

13
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:04,723
Right out of town, US 550 switchbacks up into the Uncompahgre Gorge, carved straight into the canyon wall.

14
00:01:04,723 --> 00:01:06,779
Drivers, eyes on the road.

15
00:01:06,779 --> 00:01:09,310
Passengers, eyes on those views!

16
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:15,469
This is Bear Creek Falls, and yes, the highway goes right over the top of it!

17
00:01:15,469 --> 00:01:20,070
Pull into the lot just past the bridge and walk out to the overlook.

18
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:26,514
Up through the gorge and into Ironton Park, where the old mining country begins!

19
00:01:26,514 --> 00:01:33,725
Look for the ghost town of Ironton, and the Yankee Girl Mine's wooden headframe right beside the highway.

20
00:01:33,725 --> 00:01:40,180
Then those rusty red peaks start showing up, and that's your sign: Red Mountain Pass is close!

21
00:01:41,130 --> 00:01:42,475
Red Mountain Pass!

22
00:01:42,475 --> 00:01:48,306
Eleven thousand and eighteen feet, the very top of the Million Dollar Highway.

23
00:01:48,306 --> 00:01:52,865
And here's a fun one: nobody agrees where the name came from.

24
00:01:52,865 --> 00:01:53,986
Building costs?

25
00:01:53,986 --> 00:01:55,631
Gold in the road fill?

26
00:01:55,631 --> 00:02:00,190
Or a driver who said, never again, not for a million dollars!

27
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:13,844
Now it's all downhill along Mineral Creek, and there's one more detour to know about: Ice Lake Basin, one of the most famous hikes in Colorado, starts just west of Silverton.

28
00:02:13,844 --> 00:02:15,450
Then, here comes town!

29
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,216
We made it to Silverton!

30
00:02:18,216 --> 00:02:28,960
The whole town is a National Historic Landmark, and in summer the steam train from Durango pulls right into town, just like it has since 1882!

31
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:31,124
And that's it!

32
00:02:31,124 --> 00:02:40,320
24 incredible miles, from Ouray all the way to Silverton, topping out at 11,018 feet on Red Mountain Pass.

33
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:44,759
Okay, here's everything you need to plan this drive yourself.

34
00:02:44,759 --> 00:02:46,990
Pause right here and grab a screenshot!

35
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,966
Thanks so much for riding along!

36
00:02:51,966 --> 00:02:55,740
Hit subscribe, and I'll see you on the road to Durango!
